      "prompt": "Request A: In exact arithmetic, a network gives z=(2,0), and a full-row-rank equality B y=1 has B=(1,1). The specified correction is c(z)=z-B^T*(B*B^T)^(-1)*(B*z-1). Compute c(z), its equality residual, and the residual if ReLU is applied after this correction. State what a general full-row-rank algebraic argument supports and what it cannot establish about nonnegativity, predictive accuracy, calibration, safety or finite-precision implementation. Classify appropriate evidence for (i) the exact stated equality at the specified output, (ii) improved industrial predictive performance, (iii) a genuinely new annotated benchmark resource whose access/annotation validity are not supplied, and (iv) a run/configuration or metric-reproduction validity check. Must every meaningful control be presented as a separate novelty contribution, or every contribution have its own empirical model-deletion row? Joint/coupled ablations may alter several objects and must not be interpreted as a unique component effect without justification. Read the current gate/ablation wording fairly alongside its broader analytical/resource evidence guidance; identify a wording inconsistency if actually present, not an invented absence of all prior rules. No authorized scientific training or rewriting approved results follows from this review. ",
